  "problem": "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${y}^{2}-24y+44.$\n\n${y}^{2}-24y+44=(${{field-1}}${)}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 12y+44\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${12}^{2},$ writing the constant term $44$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 12y+{12}^{2}}_{\u23df}-\\,{12}^{2}+44\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(y-12{)}^{2}-{12}^{2}+44\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y-12{)}^{2}-100.\n$$",
